  ],
  "summary": "Amadey is a modular malware loader and Stealc a MaaS infostealer, both sold as services with affiliate-run C&C panels; ESET clustered hundreds of samples using embedded RC4 keys, C&C URL random paths, and build identifiers ('sd' for Amadey, 'build' for Stealc) to support Operation Endgame. Amadey beacons over HTTP with an initial 'st=s' POST, receives RC4-encrypted task lists delimited by <c> and <d>, and can deploy stealer, clipper, hVNC and proxy modules; Stealc speaks RC4-encrypted JSON containing build/hwid, an access_token session key and steal_* configuration flags. Both families check the victim's keyboard layout and abort on CIS-country locales.",
